'' Function-like macros and token builtins must expand inside a '#if' condition.
'' They did not, so '#if TWO( a, b ) = 2' silently took the FALSE branch -- a wrong
'' answer with no diagnostic, which is the worst kind.
''
'' The golden PINNED HALF THE BUG for a while: the '__FB_ARG_COUNT__' branch was
'' recorded as not taken. The count was produced correctly and then read back as
'' whatever byte sat at the invocation site, because a re-lexed NUMERIC literal
'' recorded no text span -- only strings did -- and its loc had been repointed at the
'' use site for diagnostics.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-tokens=pp tests/pp/src/ifexpand.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0308
'' GOLDEN: expected/ifexpand.out
